Subject: [PATCH] spi: qpic-snand: do not keep a freed ECC context in qspi->ecc

The OOB layout callbacks, block erase and the raw read/write paths take
the ECC setup from qspi->ecc. That pointer was only updated when a page
I/O was prepared, and the ECC context it pointed to is freed when the
SPI NAND probe fails or is deferred.

On boards whose flash has an OTP area (ESMT F50D1G41LB on newer Xiaomi
BE7000 units) the first probe reads OTP pages before it is deferred
waiting for SMEM, so qspi->ecc keeps pointing at the freed context. The
second probe then counts the free OOB bytes from freed memory, gets a
garbage negative value and fails, the MTD partitions never appear and
the kernel waits for its root device forever. It happened on roughly
one boot in three.

Point qspi->ecc at the new context as soon as it is set up, and clear
it when that context is freed.

Signed-off-by: Timofey Maykov <itnitro@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/spi/spi-qpic-snand.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/spi-qpic-snand.c
@@ -384,6 +384,13 @@
 	memset(snandc->qspi->oob_buf, 0xff, mtd->writesize + mtd->oobsize);
 
 	nand->ecc.ctx.priv = ecc_cfg;
+	/*
+	 * The OOB layout callbacks and the raw paths read the ECC setup from
+	 * qspi->ecc, which was only updated on the first page I/O. Before
+	 * that it could still point at the context of an earlier probe that
+	 * got deferred and freed.
+	 */
+	snandc->qspi->ecc = ecc_cfg;
 	snandc->qspi->mtd = mtd;
 
 	ecc_cfg->bbm_size = 1;
@@ -472,8 +479,13 @@
 
 static void qcom_spi_ecc_cleanup_ctx_pipelined(struct nand_device *nand)
 {
+	struct qcom_nand_controller *snandc = nand_to_qcom_snand(nand);
 	struct qpic_ecc *ecc_cfg = nand_to_ecc_ctx(nand);
 
+	/* do not leave the controller pointing at the context freed here */
+	if (snandc->qspi->ecc == ecc_cfg)
+		snandc->qspi->ecc = NULL;
+
 	kfree(ecc_cfg);
 }
 
